---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = "Mensa-Style Practice Test: High-Difficulty Non-Verbal Reasoning | FreeIQExam";
const description = "Practice high-difficulty visual reasoning and spatial pattern problems calibrated to the top 2nd percentile (IQ 130+). Unofficial practice resource.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Header currentPath="/mensa-iq-test-practice" />

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-5xl w-full mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 sm:py-12 flex flex-col gap-10">
    
    <!-- Mandatory Top Legal Disclaimer Callout -->
    <aside class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/40 border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-900 text-xs sm:text-sm text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-200 font-medium">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-bold text-base mt-0.5">!</span>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Mandatory Non-Affiliation Notice:</strong> FreeIQExam is an independent educational and self-assessment platform. This practice resource is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Mensa International or any national Mensa organization. Official qualification requires taking a proctored clinical battery administered by Mensa or a certified psychologist.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <!-- Hero Header -->
    <header class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-950/50 border border-purple-200 dark:border-purple-900 text-xs font-mono font-medium text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 mb-4">
        <span>TOP 2ND PERCENTILE PRACTICE &bull; HIGH CEILING (IQ 130+)</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-heading font-extrabold text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight leading-tight mb-4">
        Mensa-Style Cognitive Practice Test
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
        Challenge yourself with high-ceiling non-verbal matrix induction and 3D spatial rotation problems designed to differentiate abilities in the 98th percentile range.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- The 98th Percentile Threshold Explained -->
    <section class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50/80 dark:bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 shadow-xs">
      <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white mb-3">
        Understanding the Mensa Qualifying Threshold
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Founded in 1946, Mensa accepts individuals who score at or above the 98th percentile on an approved, standardized intelligence examination. Because different psychometric scales use distinct standard deviations, the qualifying cutoff number varies:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-zinc-400 uppercase">Wechsler Scale</span>
          <p class="font-heading font-extrabold text-3xl text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 my-1">130 IQ</p>
          <span class="text-xs text-zinc-500 font-mono">Standard Deviation 15</span>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-zinc-400 uppercase">Stanford-Binet Scale</span>
          <p class="font-heading font-extrabold text-3xl text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 my-1">132 IQ</p>
          <span class="text-xs text-zinc-500 font-mono">Standard Deviation 16</span>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-zinc-400 uppercase">Cattell Culture Fair</span>
          <p class="font-heading font-extrabold text-3xl text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 my-1">148 IQ</p>
          <span class="text-xs text-zinc-500 font-mono">Standard Deviation 24</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 mt-4 text-center">
        Note: While the numerical score varies based on scale variance, all three scores denote the identical statistical cutoff: higher than 98% of the general population.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- High-Difficulty Puzzle Walkthrough -->
    <section class="p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 shadow-xs">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-2">
        Ceiling Item Anatomy
      </span>
      <h3 class="font-heading font-bold text-xl text-zinc-950 dark:text-white mb-3">
        Walkthrough: Deconstructing a High-Ceiling Composite Matrix
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        What separates standard cognitive items from 98th percentile ceiling problems is rule concurrency. Mensa-level problems frequently overlay two to three simultaneous transformation rules:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200/60 dark:border-zinc-800/60">
          <strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white font-semibold">Layer 1: Perimeter Latin Square</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">The outer bounding shape cycles through circle, square, and diamond independently of inner components.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200/60 dark:border-zinc-800/60">
          <strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white font-semibold">Layer 2: Internal Boolean XOR Cancellation</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">Line segments inside the frame superimpose and cancel out when overlapping across column transitions.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200/60 dark:border-zinc-800/60">
          <strong class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white font-semibold">Layer 3: Directional Enantiomer Inversion</strong>
          <p class="mt-1">The orientation of asymmetric corner notches flips polarity based on whether the row parity is odd or even.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Test Taking Strategies for Timed Cognitive Tests -->
    <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 sm:gap-6">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
        <span class="font-mono text-blue-600 font-bold text-lg mb-2 block">01</span>
        <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Time Budgeting</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">
          On a 20-minute, 24-question assessment, early items require approximately 25 seconds, allowing you to reserve 75 to 90 seconds for high-ceiling items 18 through 24.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
        <span class="font-mono text-indigo-600 font-bold text-lg mb-2 block">02</span>
        <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Eliminate Foils First</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">
          Distractors are engineered around specific cognitive traps: incomplete rule applications and directional reversals. Eliminating obvious traps leaves the unique logical solution.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-3xl bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/40 border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80">
        <span class="font-mono text-purple-600 font-bold text-lg mb-2 block">03</span>
        <h4 class="font-heading font-bold text-base text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Track 3D Chirality</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">
          In mental cube rotation, mirror enantiomers look deceptively identical. Always verify the clockwise order of faces around a shared vertex corner.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Bottom Legal Disclaimer Callout -->
    <aside class="p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-900 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 text-xs text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
      <p class="leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Mensa is a registered trademark of Mensa International Limited. FreeIQExam has no connection to Mensa, and completion of this practice test does not confer membership or constitute an official evaluation.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <!-- Assessment CTA -->
    <section class="p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-tr from-blue-600 via-indigo-600 to-purple-600 text-white text-center shadow-lg relative overflow-hidden">
      <h2 class="font-heading font-extrabold text-2xl sm:text-4xl mb-3 tracking-tight">
        Take the Full 24-Item Assessment
      </h2>
      <p class="text-blue-100 text-sm sm:text-base max-w-xl mx-auto mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        Test your fluid logic under strict 20-minute timed conditions. Get your estimated standard score (SD 15) and population percentile ranking immediately.
      </p>
      <a 
        href="/test" 
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-8 py-4 rounded-full text-base font-bold text-zinc-950 bg-white hover:bg-zinc-100 transition-all shadow-md hover:scale-102 active:scale-98"
      >
        <span>Start Timed Assessment</span>
        <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5L21 12m0 0l-7.5 7.5M21 12H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
